# Strapi Cloud production news — tenant, categories, slugs, and cover repair

## Problem (symptoms)

- Production news page shows **“No articles”** while local works.
- **Tenant filter** returns 0 when published rows lack `articles_tenant_lnk` (draft may have tenant; published does not).
- **Category sections empty** when production slugs are `Main-News` but frontend filters `main-news`.
- Covers/ads show placeholders after Cloud push or when S3 keys point at the wrong prefix.

## Root causes

1. **Strapi 5 Draft & Publish**: draft and published are separate DB rows; **relation link tables are not always copied on publish**.
2. **Category slug casing**: UID fields stored with wrong casing break `filters[category][slug][$eq]=main-news`.
3. **Media stripped / wrong S3 prefix** on tenant push: covers need durable S3 register, then tenant re-link (see gotchas below).

## Enforcement (code — requires Strapi Cloud deploy)

| Layer | File | Behavior |
|-------|------|----------|
| Article lifecycles | [`src/api/article/content-types/article/lifecycles.js`](mdc:src/api/article/content-types/article/lifecycles.js) | `beforeCreate` / `beforeUpdate`: assign tenant from editor-tenant mapping |
| Slug lifecycles + middleware | [`src/utils/normalize-slug.js`](mdc:src/utils/normalize-slug.js), per-type `lifecycles.js`, [`src/bootstrap.js`](mdc:src/bootstrap.js) | All UID `slug` fields → lowercase kebab-case on save; optional `STRICT_KEBAB_SLUG=1` rejects invalid slugs with a validation error |
| Publish middleware | [`src/bootstrap.js`](mdc:src/bootstrap.js) `registerTenantPublishMiddleware()` | **Before** publish: ensure draft has tenant; **after** publish: copy tenant link to published row |
| Shared helpers | [`src/utils/tenant-assignment.js`](mdc:src/utils/tenant-assignment.js) | Editor→tenant resolution, link-table ensure/copy |
| Editor RBAC | [`src/bootstrap.js`](mdc:src/bootstrap.js) `registerTenantDocumentMiddleware()` | Tenant-scoped find/update for editor role |

**Tenant-scoped UIDs** (publish middleware): article, advertisement-slot, flash-news-item, directory-home, and all directory collection types listed in `registerTenantPublishMiddleware`.

## News push gotchas (articles + ads)

- **`push:tenant-to-cloud` publish resets `publishedAt` to “now”.** After pushing articles, restore historical dates from local:
  ```bash
  npm run sync:article-published-dates-cloud -- --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
  ```
  Uses `POST /api/migration/fix-published` (knex) so Document Service publish does not overwrite dates again.
- **Cover PUT can drop tenant/category (and previously wiped title/slug).** After S3 article covers, re-link tenants. Prefer the orchestrator:
  ```bash
  npm run repair:cloud-news-sync -- --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
  ```
  S3 linker preserves `title`/`slug`/… and maps category by **Cloud slug**; still re-run tenant fix after cover link.
- **Clean article re-upload (conflicts / full overwrite from local):** order matters — the S3 cover link **re-publishes** every article (resets `publishedAt` and drops tenant on draft + published rows), so restore dates **last**:
  1. `npm run wipe:cloud-articles-tenant -- --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2`
  2. `npm run push:tenant-to-cloud -- --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2 --types=articles --force --delay-ms=80`
  3. `npm run push:collection-images-s3-to-cloud -- --collection=articles --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2 --skip-api`
  4. Re-link tenant on the **new** documents only (draft: `PUT /api/articles/:documentId?status=draft` with `{ tenant }` — keeps title/slug/cover/category; published: `fix-published` with `tenantDocumentId`)
  5. `npm run sync:article-published-dates-cloud -- --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2`
- **Duplicate published rows:** older `fix-published` builds also stamped `published_at` on the **draft** row, so the Content API returned every article twice once the draft had a tenant. Fixed in [`src/index.js`](mdc:src/index.js): drafts stay `NULL`, extra stamped rows are reset (`results.draftsReset`). Check: tenant-filtered `/api/articles` total must equal unique `documentId` count.
- ❌ **Do not** run `scripts/repair-production-article-tenant.mjs` on production — it PUTs the target tenant onto **every** article document (all tenants). Use `repair-production-article-tenant-published.mjs` (only drafts already on the tenant) or targeted documentIds.
- **Local ads/flash scrape:** `npm run seed:ads-flash-catholicatenews -- --tenants=tenant_demo_002,mosc_malankara_orthodox_2`
- **Durable covers/ads media:** use S3 strategy A — [strapi-cloud-production-durable-s3-image-upload-not-ephemeral-uploads.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/strapi-cloud-production-durable-s3-image-upload-not-ephemeral-uploads.mdc) (`--collection=articles` / `advertisement-slots`, `--skip-api`).
- **S3 register with `prod/` prefix while local media lives under `dev/`** creates Cloud URLs that **403** (object missing under prod). `push-collection-images-s3` now copies remote `dev/` bytes into the prod key before register. Emergency repair:
  ```bash
  node scripts/repair-cloud-ad-s3-from-dev.js
  ```
- Bucket has **ACLs disabled** — do not pass `ACL: public-read` on PutObject; see [strapi-aws-s3-upload-omit-acl-when-bucket-owner-enforced.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/strapi-aws-s3-upload-omit-acl-when-bucket-owner-enforced.mdc).
- **Full news Cloud runbook:** [news-production-cloud-push-prd.html](mdc:documentation/front_end_based_collection_types_import/production_cloud_data_push/news-production-cloud-push-prd.html)

## One-time Cloud repair (no new deploy required for endpoint)

Uses existing **`POST /api/migration/fix-published`** in [`src/index.js`](mdc:src/index.js):

```json
{
  "tenantDocumentId": "<tenant documentId from /api/tenants>",
  "articles": [{ "documentId": "...", "uid": "api::article.article" }]
}
```

Auth: `Authorization: Bearer` = `STRAPI_CLOUD_API_TOKEN` or `STRAPI_MIGRATION_TOKEN`.

